# 🧠 AI Recruitment Intelligence

Full-stack platform that scores resume-to-job fit, finds skill gaps, ranks candidates in bulk, and runs
**voice-based mock interviews** with per-answer scoring, speech analytics and a final hiring recommendation.

## Features
| Area | What it does |
|---|---|
| ATS analysis | TF-IDF / cosine-similarity scoring, skill-gap detection, job matching, learning plan |
| AI interview | Resume- and JD-aware questions, difficulty levels, per-answer scores and feedback, final report |
| Voice | Text-to-speech questions + Whisper (Groq) speech-to-text answers, works in all modern browsers |
| Speech analytics | Words per minute, filler-word detection, pace feedback |
| STAR coach | Checks behavioural answers for Situation / Task / Action / Result |
| Timer + proctoring | Per-question timer, tab-switch detection |
| Accounts | Register / login (JWT, PBKDF2-hashed passwords), SQLite interview history with progress chart |
| Recruiter tools | Bulk ranking of up to 20 resumes against one job description |
| Resume rewriter | Job-targeted bullet rewrites (never invents facts) |
| Reports | One-click PDF interview report |
| Engineering | Rate limiting, request logging, JSON error handling, pytest suite, Docker, GitHub Actions CI |

## Architecture
```mermaid
flowchart LR
  B[Browser: HTML/JS, Chart.js, MediaRecorder] -->|REST + JWT| A[FastAPI]
  A --> S[scoring.py: TF-IDF / cosine]
  A --> L[llm.py: Groq LLM]
  A --> W[Groq Whisper STT]
  A --> D[(SQLite)]
```

## Run locally
```powershell
python -m venv venv ; .\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install -r requirements.txt
# .env in the project root:
#   LLM_PROVIDER=groq
#   GROQ_API_KEY=your_key
#   LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
#   JWT_SECRET=a-long-random-string
cd backend
uvicorn main:app --reload
```
Open http://127.0.0.1:8000

## Tests
```powershell
cd backend ; python -m pytest tests -q
```

## Docker
```bash
docker build -t ai-recruitment .
docker run -p 8000:8000 --env-file .env ai-recruitment
```

## Deploy (Render / Railway)
Create a Web Service from this repo using the Dockerfile and add the environment variables above.
Note: SQLite data resets on free hosts that have no persistent disk; use a Postgres database for production.

## API overview
`POST /api/analyze` · `POST /api/interview/start|answer` · `GET /api/interview/report/{id}` ·
`POST /api/auth/register|login` · `GET /api/history` · `POST /api/history/save` ·
`POST /api/speech/analyze` · `POST /api/star/check` · `POST /api/transcribe` ·
`POST /api/bulk-rank` · `POST /api/rewrite-resume` · `POST /api/report/pdf`

## Limitations / roadmap
In-memory interview sessions (move to the database), adaptive difficulty, webcam proctoring, Postgres.